Changed: FiniteElement::get_prolongation_matrix() and
FiniteElement::get_restriction_matrix() now have versions which take a
RefinementChoice: these are the virtual functions which derived classes must
override. The versions which take a RefinementCase are no longer virtual and
are deprecated (calls like `fe.get_prolongation_matrix(child)` continue to
work). Furthermore, the protected member variables FiniteElement::prolongation
and FiniteElement::restriction were renamed to
FiniteElement::prolongation_matrices and FiniteElement::restriction_matrices
since they are now indexed by ReferenceCell::refinement_choice_index(), which
differs from the previous indexing for simplices, wedges, and pyramids. As a
result, finite element classes defined outside of deal.II which override the
old functions or access these variables directly no longer compile and must
be updated.
<br>
(David Wells, 2026/11/14)
